## 20. First launch offline sends the user to the game — permanently

**Symptom:** OneLink install with the radio off. The app shows the game, and
after Wi-Fi returns it keeps showing the game on every future launch.

**Cause:** the offline branch of the first decision routed to the game, and the
negative verdict was persisted as the mode. The mode is by contract permanent,
so the paid user is locked out for the life of the install.

**Fix:** offline on an undecided first launch → the no-wifi screen **on the
first frame** (instant `activeNetwork` check before `setContentView`), nothing
started, nothing persisted; the offline screen relaunches the router when the
link returns. And persist `NATIVE` only when the endpoint actually answered AND
the request carried attribution (`kotlin_launch_flow.mdc` §4–5).

---

## 21. `onCreateWindow` with the same WebView (CRASH)

**Symptom:** `IllegalArgumentException: Parent WebView cannot host its own
popup window`. Reproduced on the third page of a test site's "next page" chain.

**Cause:** `setSupportMultipleWindows(true)` plus
`transport.webView = view` — the parent WebView cannot be its own popup host.

**Fix:** `setSupportMultipleWindows(false)`; `window.open` then loads in place.
Only if popups are truly required, create a separate throwaway WebView for the
transport and forward its first URL to the main view.

